WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.632
Real data does not always contain valid values If
Python tries to convert the

00:00:05.658 --> 00:00:10.211
text abc into a number the conversion fails because
the text does not represent a

00:00:10.224 --> 00:00:15.780
numeric value The example uses a small try and
except structure so

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:21.467
the program can respond to the problem instead of
stopping unexpectedly We will study error

00:00:21.493 --> 00:00:25.888
handling in more detail later so you do not need to
memorize this syntax now

00:00:27.615 --> 00:00:33.115
The main lesson is analytical rather than syntactic
never assume every incoming value is valid

00:00:34.051 --> 00:00:39.709
Data validation is part of reliable analysis Try
replacing abc with forty

00:00:39.736 --> 00:00:42.749
two point five and notice that the conversion then
succeeds
